{
  "id": "internalization",
  "term": "internalization",
  "definition": "In this social-psychology context, internalization means taking in and adopting appearance ideals, such as being very thin/low in body fat or looking muscular/athletic, as personal standards. In the study packet, stronger internalization was linked with more body-focused anxiety and monitoring, and with greater avoidance of physical activity or sport because of appearance concerns.",
