      "reasons": [
        "The definition states that internalization involves “adopting … as personal standards,” but the packet describes thin/low body fat internalization (TLB) and muscular/athletic internalization (MA) and their associations with APAS, social physique anxiety, and body surveillance; it does not explicitly define internalization as “personal standards.”",
        "The definition’s framing that avoidance occurs “because of appearance concerns” goes beyond what the packet explicitly states; the packet reports associations with “appearance-related avoidance of physical activity and sport (APAS)” and appearance-evaluative settings, but it does not spell out the causal rationale “because of appearance concerns.”"
      ],
